2:T418,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article","headline":"How to Reprogram Your Reticular Activating System (RAS) to Filter for Success","description":"Learn how your Reticular Activating System (RAS) filters 11 million bits of data per second and how to reprogram your neural filter using repetition and emotional state.","datePublished":"2025-02-01","dateModified":"2026-11-19","articleSection":"Neuroscience","keywords":"reticular activating system reprogramming, 11 million bits of information brain filter, neuroscience of manifestation, how the RAS works, programming the gatekeeper, subconscious filter perception","mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://vibehyr.com/blog/reticular-activating-system-reality"},"author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Keisha Solomon","jobTitle":"Founder & Master Architect, Vibe Hyr"},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Vibe Hyr","url":"https://vibehyr.com","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://vibehyr.com/icons/icon-512.png"}},"image":"https://vibehyr.com/images/og-image.png"}7:["slug","reticular-activating-system-reality","d"]
0:["3liVyMVjhg1tkB_fuWghV",[[["",{"children":["blog",{"children":[["slug","reticular-activating-system-reality","d"],{"children":["__PAGE__?{\"slug\":\"reticular-activating-system-reality\"}",{}]}]}]},"$undefined","$undefined",true],["",{"children":["blog",{"children":[["slug","reticular-activating-system-reality","d"],{"children":["__PAGE__",{},[["$L1",[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$2"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://vibehyr.com\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Blog\",\"item\":\"https://vibehyr.com/blog\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":3,\"name\":\"Your Brain Filters Reality — Here's How to Program It\",\"item\":\"https://vibehyr.com/blog/reticular-activating-system-reality\"}]}"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How does the Reticular Activating System (RAS) affect what you experience?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Your sensory organs take in roughly 11 million bits of data every second, but your conscious prefrontal cortex can process only about 40 to 50 bits. The RAS decides which 50 bits reach your awareness based on your dominant beliefs, fears, and identity assumptions — literally hiding opportunities that contradict your current self-concept.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What are the two fastest ways to reprogram the RAS?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"The RAS responds to (1) high-frequency repetition (such as morning identity directives and nightly revision) and (2) limbic emotional intensity (feeling the somatic reality of a state during SATS rather than repeating empty words).\"}}]}"}}],["$","$L3",null,{}],["$","main",null,{"className":"pt-[68px] min-h-screen","children":[["$","section",null,{"className":"py-14 px-6 md:px-14 border-b border-white/8 relative","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"absolute left-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-1 bg-orange-DEFAULT"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-3xl mx-auto pl-4","children":[["$","nav",null,{"aria-label":"Breadcrumb","className":"mb-8","children":["$","ol",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-[0.52rem] tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-grey-dark flex-wrap","children":[["$","li",null,{"children":["$","$L4",null,{"href":"/","className":"hover:text-orange-DEFAULT transition-colors","children":"Home"}]}],["$","li",null,{"children":"/"}],["$","li",null,{"children":["$","$L4",null,{"href":"/blog","className":"hover:text-orange-DEFAULT transition-colors","children":"Blog"}]}],["$","li",null,{"children":"/"}],["$","li",null,{"className":"text-orange-DEFAULT truncate max-w-xs","aria-current":"page","children":"Neuroscience"}]]}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-3 flex-wrap mb-6","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-[0.55rem] tracking-[0.3em] uppercase text-orange-DEFAULT","children":"Neuroscience"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-[0.48rem] tracking-[0.18em] uppercase px-2.5 py-0.5 bg-white/[0.04] border border-white/10 text-grey-DEFAULT","children":"Personal Mastery"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-1.5 font-mono text-[0.55rem] tracking-[0.1em] text-grey-dark","children":[["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":10,"height":10,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-clock","children":[["$","circle","1mglay",{"cx":"12","cy":"12","r":"10"}],["$","polyline","68esgv",{"points":"12 6 12 12 16 14"}],"$undefined"]}]," ",6," min read"]}]]}],["$","h1",null,{"className":"font-display text-[clamp(2.2rem,5vw,4rem)] leading-[0.95] tracking-[0.02em] text-white mb-5","children":"Your Brain Filters Reality — Here's How to Program It"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"font-body italic text-grey-DEFAULT text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6","children":"Your Reticular Activating System receives 11 million bits of data per second and lets only 50 into conscious awareness. You can decide which 50. This is the neuroscience of manifestation."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-center justify-between flex-wrap gap-4 pt-5 border-t border-white/10 font-mono text-[0.5rem] tracking-widest text-grey-dark","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":["By ",["$","span",null,{"className":"text-white font-medium","children":"Keisha Solomon"}]," · ","Founder & Master Architect, Vibe Hyr"]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":["Published ",["$","time",null,{"dateTime":"2025-02-01","children":"January 31, 2025"}]]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-[#dfbd8b]","children":["Updated ",["$","time",null,{"dateTime":"2026-11-19","children":"November 18, 2026"}]]}]]}]]}]]}]]}],["$","article",null,{"className":"py-12 px-6 md:px-14","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-3xl mx-auto","children":[["$","nav",null,{"aria-label":"Table of Contents","className":"mb-10 p-6 bg-black-2 border border-orange-DEFAULT/25","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-[0.52rem] tracking-[0.22em] uppercase text-orange-DEFAULT mb-3","children":[["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":13,"height":13,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-book-open","children":[["$","path","vv98re",{"d":"M2 3h6a4 4 0 0 1 4 4v14a3 3 0 0 0-3-3H2z"}],["$","path","1cyq3y",{"d":"M22 3h-6a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v14a3 3 0 0 1 3-3h7z"}],"$undefined"]}],"In This Guide"]}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-x-6 gap-y-2","children":[["$","li","the-filter-between-you-and-reality",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"#the-filter-between-you-and-reality","className":"font-body text-sm text-grey-DEFAULT hover:text-orange-DEFAULT transition-colors flex items-baseline gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-[0.5rem] text-orange-DEFAULT/80","children":["01","."]}],["$","span",null,{"children":"The Filter Between You and Reality"}]]}]}],["$","li","how-the-ras-gets-programmed",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"#how-the-ras-gets-programmed","className":"font-body text-sm text-grey-DEFAULT hover:text-orange-DEFAULT transition-colors flex items-baseline gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-[0.5rem] text-orange-DEFAULT/80","children":["02","."]}],["$","span",null,{"children":"How the RAS Gets Programmed"}]]}]}],["$","li","the-car-analogy",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"#the-car-analogy","className":"font-body text-sm text-grey-DEFAULT hover:text-orange-DEFAULT transition-colors flex items-baseline gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-[0.5rem] text-orange-DEFAULT/80","children":["03","."]}],["$","span",null,{"children":"The Car Analogy"}]]}]}],["$","li","reprogramming-the-filter",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"#reprogramming-the-filter","className":"font-body text-sm text-grey-DEFAULT hover:text-orange-DEFAULT transition-colors flex items-baseline gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-[0.5rem] text-orange-DEFAULT/80","children":["04","."]}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Reprogramming the Filter"}]]}]}],["$","li","practical-implications",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"#practical-implications","className":"font-body text-sm text-grey-DEFAULT hover:text-orange-DEFAULT transition-colors flex items-baseline gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-[0.5rem] text-orange-DEFAULT/80","children":["05","."]}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Practical Implications"}]]}]}]]}]]}],[["$","h2","0",{"id":"the-filter-between-you-and-reality","className":"scroll-mt-24 font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-[0.03em] text-white mt-12 mb-4","children":"The Filter Between You and Reality"}],["$","p","1",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["Right now, as you read this, your brain is receiving an incomprehensible amount of information. The pressure of the chair against your body. The ambient sounds in the room. The temperature of the air. The slight tension in your shoulders. Thousands of micro-inputs, every second."]}],["$","p","2",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["You're not aware of most of them. And that's by design."]}],["$","p","3",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["The Reticular Activating System (RAS) is a bundle of nerve fibers at the base of your brainstem. It acts as a filter, allowing only a tiny fraction of incoming data into conscious awareness. The criteria it uses to decide what gets through? ",["$","strong","1",{"className":"text-white font-semibold","children":"What you've told it matters."}],""]}],["$","h2","4",{"id":"how-the-ras-gets-programmed","className":"scroll-mt-24 font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-[0.03em] text-white mt-12 mb-4","children":"How the RAS Gets Programmed"}],["$","p","5",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["Every repeated thought, strong emotion, and deeply held belief trains your RAS. If you've spent years believing money is hard to come by, your RAS has been trained to filter for evidence of scarcity — and to filter ",["$","em","1",{"className":"text-white/90 italic","children":"out"}]," opportunities. Not because the opportunities don't exist, but because your RAS has classified them as irrelevant."]}],["$","p","6",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["This is why two people can walk through the same city and have completely different experiences. One sees danger. One sees possibility. The city is the same. The filters are different."]}],["$","h2","7",{"id":"the-car-analogy","className":"scroll-mt-24 font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-[0.03em] text-white mt-12 mb-4","children":"The Car Analogy"}],["$","p","8",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["You've experienced this. The moment you start thinking about buying a specific car — say, a white Tesla — you suddenly see white Teslas everywhere. They were always there. Your RAS simply wasn't flagging them."]}],["$","p","9",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["This is precisely how the Law of Assumption works at a neurological level. When you assume a state — when you deeply inhabit the feeling of the wish fulfilled — you reprogram the RAS to select for evidence of that state in the environment."]}],["$","h2","10",{"id":"reprogramming-the-filter","className":"scroll-mt-24 font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-[0.03em] text-white mt-12 mb-4","children":"Reprogramming the Filter"}],["$","p","11",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["The RAS responds to two things most powerfully:"]}],["$","p","12",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["",["$","strong","1",{"className":"text-white font-semibold","children":"1. Repetition."}]," The more frequently a thought or belief is activated, the more the RAS treats it as a priority filter. This is why the Nightly Revision Journal works — you're creating deliberate, repeated impressions."]}],["$","p","13",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["",["$","strong","1",{"className":"text-white font-semibold","children":"2. Emotional intensity."}]," The RAS is strongly coupled to the limbic system (the emotional brain). Thoughts with strong emotional charge are flagged as important and filter through more easily. This is why feeling — not just thinking — is central to SATS."]}],["$","h2","14",{"id":"practical-implications","className":"scroll-mt-24 font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-[0.03em] text-white mt-12 mb-4","children":"Practical Implications"}],["$","p","15",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["If you want to change what you experience in life, you must change what your RAS is looking for. And to change what your RAS looks for, you must change the programming: the repeated, emotionally charged states you inhabit."]}],["$","p","16",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["This is not positive thinking. It's neural reprogramming through deliberate assumption."]}],["$","p","17",{"className":"font-body text-grey-DEFAULT leading-relaxed mb-5 text-[1.05rem]","children":["The architecture of your reality is built by the filters in your mind. Vibe Hyr exists to help you become the architect."]}]],["$","section",null,{"aria-labelledby":"faq-heading","className":"mt-16 pt-10 border-t border-white/10","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-[0.52rem] tracking-[0.25em] uppercase text-orange-DEFAULT mb-2","children":[["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":13,"height":13,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-circle-help","children":[["$","circle","1mglay",{"cx":"12","cy":"12","r":"10"}],["$","path","1u773s",{"d":"M9.09 9a3 3 0 0 1 5.83 1c0 2-3 3-3 3"}],["$","path","p32p05",{"d":"M12 17h.01"}],"$undefined"]}],"Key Questions Answered"]}],[